# Source: https://genome.ucsc.edu/FAQ/FAQformat.html#format1
#   https://github.com/arq5x/bedtools2/issues/998
# Symptom: name field (col 4) contains Latin-1 (ISO-8859-1) encoded bytes
#   that are not valid UTF-8; arises from sample names in clinical databases
#   that use ISO-8859-1 (e.g. French accented characters: eacute = 0xe9).
#   Tools that validate fields as UTF-8 raise a decoding error; tools that
#   pass through binary data may silently corrupt downstream JSON/XML outputs.
#   The 0xe9 byte (e with acute in Latin-1) triggers "invalid continuation byte"
#   in Python str.decode("utf-8").
chr1	100	200	echantillon_témoin	0	+
chr1	300	400	séquence_001	255	-
